<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qvarqvare II Jaqeli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1498</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Qvarqvare II of Samtskhe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qvarqvare II Jaqeli was atabeg of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samtskhe">Samtskhe</a>, a principality in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, from 1451 to 1498. Seeking independence from the Georgian crown, he captured King George VIII in 1465, which helped bring about the break-up of the united Kingdom of Georgia. He then supported rival claimants to keep the kings weak and made Samtskhe virtually independent.</p></div>
